WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.960
A signature looks familiar,

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.560
but where exactly do the strokes differ?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.040
In Avera, start a case.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.100
Set the document type and priority,

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.160
then add the signatures

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.260
you want to compare.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.920
Four reference signatures,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.560
one questioned sample.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.740
Capture the handwriting,

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.300
and Avera prepares the images for comparison.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.660
Start with the heat map.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.300
The bounding box shows the

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.540
outer edge of the ink.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.860
Now follow the same numbered marker across

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.820
the signatures to compare the strokes.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.780
Here, the model flags the

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.880
questioned signature as suspected.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.000
A supervisor reviews the evidence,

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.240
records a decision,

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.920
and chooses whether to allow PDF export.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.100
The case summary and stroke comparisons

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.940
come together in one report.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.360
Avera,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.240
signature analysis for review.
